---
const faqs = [
  {
    q: "How much does a website cost?",
    a: "£50 a month. That covers a custom website for your business, hosting and maintenance, content updates, Google Business Profile management and a check-in every two weeks. Your first £50 is paid when you sign up and covers your first month.",
  },
  {
    q: "Is there a minimum contract?",
    a: "Yes, 12 months. After that the plan carries on at £50 a month until you cancel. It's an ongoing service, so payments don't stop automatically after 12 months, and the website doesn't become yours unless you buy it outright.",
  },
  {
    q: "How do I cancel?",
    a: "After the first 12 months, give me 30 days' notice in writing (email is fine). If you want to leave during the first 12 months, the remaining months of the minimum term still apply. Either way, I'll give you a handover date, return your content and help move your domain before the website goes offline.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can I own my website outright?",
    a: "Yes. You can buy the website for a one-off £499. I hand over the site's files and move it to a host of your choice. From then on, my monthly services stop and hosting, updates and your Google profile are up to you.",
  },
  {
    q: "What does Google Business Profile management include?",
    a: "You add me as a manager on your profile (I never need your password). I keep your hours, services, photos and contact details accurate and post updates when they're useful. I can't promise rankings or a number of enquiries, but I make sure what customers see is right.",
  },
  {
    q: "What are the check-ins?",
    a: "Every two weeks I'll message you to ask whether anything has changed, like prices, opening hours, services or photos, and then make the updates for you.",
  },
  {
    q: "What updates are included?",
    a: "Changes to your existing pages, like text, prices, opening hours, photos and contact details. New pages, new features or a redesign are quoted separately, and only go ahead if you agree.",
  },
  {
    q: "Who owns my domain and content?",
    a: "You do. Your domain name, text, photos and logo stay yours whatever happens. While you're on the plan, you can use the website for your business. If you buy it outright, the website becomes yours too.",
  },
  {
    q: "How long does a website take?",
    a: "It varies by project, but most websites are ready within a few weeks of getting started, depending on how quickly content and feedback come together.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can you redesign my existing website?",
    a: "Yes. Redesigns are one of the most common projects — bringing an outdated or hard-to-use website up to a modern, mobile-friendly standard.",
  },
  {
    q: "Do I need to provide the written content?",
    a: "Ideally yes, since you know your business best, but I'll guide you on what's needed and can help shape and tidy up the wording where it helps.",
  },
  {
    q: "What is included in the free homepage preview?",
    a: "A first look at how your homepage could feel and read, based on the information you share. There's no cost and no obligation to continue afterwards.",
  },
  {
    q: "Will the website work properly on mobile?",
    a: "Yes. Every Stapled. website is built mobile-first and tested across different screen sizes, since most local customers will find you on their phone.",
  },
];
---

<section class="faq section" id="faq">
  <div class="container faq__inner">
    <div class="faq__intro reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
      <h2 class="faq__heading">Questions, answered.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="faq__list reveal">
      {faqs.map((item) => (
        <details class="faq__item">
          <summary>
            <span>{item.q}</span>
            <svg class="faq__chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
            </svg>
          </summary>
          <p class="text-muted">{item.a}</p>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq__inner {
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .faq__intro {
    margin-bottom: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
  }

  .faq__heading {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  .faq__list {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--colour-border);
  }

  .faq__item {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--colour-border);
    padding-block: 1.25rem;
  }

  .faq__item summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .faq__item summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .faq__chevron {
    width: 20px;
    height: 20px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    transition: transform var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }

  .faq__item[open] .faq__chevron {
    transform: rotate(180deg);
  }

  .faq__item p {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    padding-right: 2rem;
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    .faq__item p {
      animation: faq-in var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out);
    }
  }

  @keyframes faq-in {
    from {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translateY(-4px);
    }
    to {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: translateY(0);
    }
  }
</style>
